{"kind":"stack","id":"s1","title":"Environments can change","theme":{"background":"#f4f9f1","foreground":"#1d3b1f","font":"Georgia, serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-q","content":"What is an environment?"},{"type":"button","id":"c1-a","label":"All the living and non-living things around a living thing","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Only the animals that live in a forest","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c1-c","label":"A type of rock found in the ground","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"Habitat"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-e","content":"The place where a plant or animal lives and finds food, water and shelter."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-next","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"Which of these can cause a habitat to change quickly?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"A flood","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"A sunny afternoon in a park","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"A quiet night in a garden","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"Why can a forest fire be dangerous to animals?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"It destroys their food, water and shelter","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"It makes the trees grow taller","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"It makes the soil wetter","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-t","content":"A heavy storm is coming. Your pond is rising fast. What do you do?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"Check on the frogs and fish in the pond","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"Ignore it and go inside","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"You spot a frog on a rock and guide it to safe grass. Well done, you helped a living thing stay safe."},{"type":"button","id":"c6-next","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"The rising water washes over the pond edge. Some animals could not escape the flood."},{"type":"button","id":"c7-next","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-q","content":"Which living thing is most at risk when a pond floods?"},{"type":"button","id":"c8-a","label":"A frog that cannot leave the water in time","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"A rock sitting on the bank","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-c","label":"A dry leaf on the path","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-t","content":"Pollution"},{"type":"text","id":"c9-e","content":"Harmful substances added to the air, water or soil that can harm living things."},{"type":"button","id":"c9-next","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"Which of these is an example of pollution harming a river?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"Oil spilled into the water, harming fish","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"Rain falling into the river","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"Leaves floating on the surface","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-h","content":"You finished the lesson on changing environments!"},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"Well done. Environments can change, and living things sometimes need our help to stay safe."}],"actions":[]}}
